Valeria

The case study web page to which you point is one example of automatic code segmentation. I believe the code was intended to be used with transects that are approximately straight. As is indicated in the web page
> If you are fluent in ArcGIS or QGIS I recommend doing this task in the software you are familiar with at first. A simple guide to doing this task in  QGIS is here <https://www.northrivergeographic.com/qgis-split-a-line-at-an-interval> and for  ArcGIS I recommend the MGET toolbox <https://mgel.env.duke.edu/mget/>.
"st_segmentize" is not always the right tool for the job, as in your case.
